To briefly respond to one of Steve Whitrow's points:

> But Mike's model seems like an epiphenomenalist view where
> consciousness serves no purpose and simply arose as a by-product.

Consciousness or self-awareness has no relevance in "my"* model.  Self-
awareness is simply the state of mind that is associated with a mental
system that has an internal model that includes itself.  The more
complex the self-representation the higher the level of consciousness. 
The goals of a system may or may not be associated with the internal
concept of self and so is irrelevant when trying to understand the
principles of goal-orientated behaviour.  A system may have a concept
of self, but not have any goals associated with it, in the same way that
I have a concept of Mount Everest but not any goals associated with it
(unlike a mountaineer).  Eg in the doomsday weapon, which I was
imagining with a concept of self and hence self-awareness and
consciousness, but a goal, of destroying Earth, that is not associated
with itself.  Such a system I would describe as unselfish (and Fnerd as
selfish).

Mike Price                         price@price.demon.co.uk

