Subject: EYES: Keratotomy

   My glasses broke awhile ago, and I looked into getting radial
keratotomy.  I thought that perhaps the price had come down so that
I could get the operation done for under $1000, but it ain't so:
$3000 for both eyes, more if there are complications.
   So I went in to get contacts and brought up RK with my eye doctor
and he said that the radial cuts form scars which do not heal.  These
scars can cause the cornea to rupture as it gets thinner - which happens
as we age.  Since the technology for RK has only been around for about
ten years (maybe more in Russia), I think I'll wait a bit, even if I
